17592186175917 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "0f524f08-137f-56e6-8a6d-a45c3dae2635" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176103 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176103 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176626 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176103 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176103 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176628 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176103 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176103 #edb/ref 1045 "Squaring a Square Root" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176103 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186176625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176103 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176103 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176103 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "a4ff07dc-a8f7-53b1-8ab9-7a78e691a8a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176625 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176626 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176625 #edb/ref 1061 16791 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176625 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e1e25251-ada4-572c-af12-8dec4f2cc93b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176625 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186176970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176626 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176626 #edb/ref 1061 16792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176626 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8bcb8880-f2b7-5129-b867-7a66c1a6f8d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176626 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186175916 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176627 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176628 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176627 #edb/ref 1061 16793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176627 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b53578db-d74c-51c3-a032-b84c8468af3c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176627 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186176971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176628 #edb/ref 1061 16794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176628 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b246c6a3-8aeb-5a46-904f-bf555b6a6441" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176628 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186175917 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176970 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's calculate $(\\sqrt{100})^2$ by performing each operation one step at a time:\n\n$$\n(\\sqrt{\\color{blue}100})^2 = \\left(\\sqrt{{\\color{red}10}^2}\\right)^2 = ({\\color{red}10})^2 = {\\color{blue}100}\n$$\n\nNotice that the squaring the square root gives the number under the square root:\n\n$$\n\\left( \\sqrt{100} \\right)^2 = 100\n$$\n\nThis result holds in general for any non-negative number. If $\\color{blue}\\square$ is any positive number or zero, then\n\n$$\n(\\sqrt{\\color{blue}\\square})^2 = {\\color{blue}\\square}\\,.\n$$\n\nThe square and the square root cancel each other out, and we're left with the number that we started with.\n\n![](images/1f/1fa29ca192dc3fb99f4180c300aa3120064e3682361d175a698b1d457a569ba0.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176970 #edb/ref 1065 3093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176970 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "871b272d-6a05-5ad2-b443-785a6abbd186" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176970 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176971 #edb/ref 1064 "We must be careful when taking the square root of a negative number that's been squared.\n\nFor example, $\\sqrt{(-9)^2}$ is *not* equal to $-9!$ We can write this using a **not equal to** symbol $\\neq$ as\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{(-9)^2}  \\neq -9.\n$$\n\nThis is because the square root of a number can *only* be positive or zero, never negative.\nLet's work it out the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(-9)^{2}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{(-9)\\cdot (-9)} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{81} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{9}^{2}} & = \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{(-9)^2}=\\sqrt{9^2} = 9.\n$$\n\nFor any positive perfect square, we always have exactly two numbers whose squares equal that number. Here, we have\n\n$$\n9^2=81\\quad \\textrm{and} \\quad (-9)^2=81.\n$$\n\nBut *by definition* the square root is always *positive* (or zero) and *cannot* be negative. So here, $\\sqrt{81}=+9,$ and for any non-negative $\\color{blue}\\square$ we get\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{\\color{blue}\\square} \\geq 0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176971 #edb/ref 1065 3094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176971 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "27f63bb3-bf90-584e-b96c-d999c482f4e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176971 #edb/ref 1067 "The Square Root of a Negative Number Squared" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179819 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179819 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180240 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179819 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179819 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186459213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179819 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186459256 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179819 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186538994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179819 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding a Missing Percent Given Two Numbers Without Simplification" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179819 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179819 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "ddf13639-8d18-5909-a26d-aeda1e011ac0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179820 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180242 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179820 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180244 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179820 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186459298 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179820 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186459309 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179820 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186544865 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179820 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding a Missing Percent Given Two Numbers Using Simplification" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179820 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179820 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "6f67408f-f019-5365-b4a0-6f60ac23cc1d" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
